#HELP_BEGIN
TCP Client (Dynamic IP) v1.0

Simpl# TCP client that matches the built-in SIMPL Windows TCP/IP Client
symbol (Connect, Connect_FB, TX$, RX$, status) except the remote host is
a serial input, not an IP-table / Address parameter. No IP-ID required.

Hold Connect high to open the socket. Release Connect to close it.
Address$ is IPv4 or a hostname. Empty Address$ will not connect.
A change to Address$ or Port_Override while Connect is high reconnects.
Port_Override greater than 0 replaces the Port parameter; 0 uses Port.

If the remote end drops while Connect is still high, the client waits
100 ms then retries (same idea as the stock client on CUZ 3.029+).

TX$ is sent as-is (no extra CR/LF) and only while connected. RX$ is a
byte pipe, chunked at 250 characters.

status (stock TCP/IP Client values):
  0d  Not connected
  1d  Waiting for connection
  2d  Connected
  3d  Connection failed
  4d  Connection broken remotely
  5d  Connection broken locally
  6d  Performing DNS lookup
  7d  DNS lookup failed
  8d  DNS lookup resolved

4-Series only. Keep Dynamic_TCP_Client.clz in this folder.

VERSION HISTORY
v1.0  2026-09-02  RGW
- Initial public module
#HELP_END

/* COMPILER DIRECTIVES */
#SYMBOL_NAME "TCP Client (Dynamic IP)"
#CATEGORY "12,41,57" // System Control, Remote System Interface, Remote Systems
#DEFAULT_VOLATILE
#ENABLE_STACK_CHECKING
#USER_SIMPLSHARP_LIBRARY "Dynamic_TCP_Client"

/* INPUTS & OUTPUTS */

DIGITAL_INPUT	Connect;
ANALOG_INPUT	Port_Override;
STRING_INPUT	Address$[64],
				_SKIP_, TX$[255];

DIGITAL_OUTPUT	Connect_FB;
ANALOG_OUTPUT	_SKIP_,
				Status;
STRING_OUTPUT	_SKIP_, RX$;

INTEGER_PARAMETER	_SKIP_, Port;

/* PROPERTIES */

#BEGIN_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES Port
	propValidUnits =		unitDecimal;
	propDefaultUnit =		unitDecimal;
	propBounds =			1d,65535d;
	propDefaultValue =		23d;
	propShortDescription =	"Remote TCP port";
#END_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES

/* GLOBAL VARIABLES */

STRING	RxBuf$[255];
STRING	Host$[64];
INTEGER	EffectivePort;
DynamicTcpClient	Core;

/* FUNCTIONS */

FUNCTION ApplyEndpoint() {
	Host$ = Address$;
	EffectivePort = Port;
	If (Port_Override > 0) {
		EffectivePort = Port_Override;
	}
}

FUNCTION DoConnect() {
	ApplyEndpoint();
	If (Len(Host$) > 0) {
		Core.Connect(Host$, EffectivePort);
	}
	Else {
		Core.Disconnect();
	}
}

/* CALLBACKS */

CALLBACK FUNCTION HandleConnection (Integer connected, Integer stat) {
	Connect_FB = connected;
	Status = stat;
}

CALLBACK FUNCTION HandleRx (String data$) {
	RxBuf$ = data$;
	RX$ = RxBuf$;
}

/* EVENTS */

CHANGE Connect {
	If (Connect = 1) {
		DoConnect();
	}
	Else {
		Core.Disconnect();
	}
}

CHANGE Address$ {
	If (Connect = 1) {
		DoConnect();
	}
}

CHANGE Port_Override {
	If (Connect = 1) {
		DoConnect();
	}
}

CHANGE TX$ {
	Core.Send(TX$);
}

/* MAIN */

FUNCTION Main() {
	RegisterDelegate(Core, OnConnectionChanged, HandleConnection);
	RegisterDelegate(Core, OnDataReceived, HandleRx);
	WaitForInitializationComplete();
	If (Connect = 1) {
		DoConnect();
	}
	Else {
		Core.PublishStatus();
	}
}
